			"Message": "refactor(Common): Standardize Workspace naming and expand error handling\n\nThis commit enforces consistent PascalCase nomenclature for the 'Workspace' concept throughout the `Common` crate, replacing the previous 'WorkSpace' casing to align with industry standards and improve API clarity. Additionally, it introduces new error variants to support specific platform features.\n\n**Refactoring Details:**\n- Renamed the `Source/WorkSpace` module directory to `Source/Workspace`.\n- Updated core traits: `WorkSpaceProvider` -> `WorkspaceProvider`, `WorkSpaceEditApplier` -> `WorkspaceEditApplier`.\n- Renamed DTOs: `WorkSpaceEditDTO` -> `WorkspaceEditDTO`.\n- Updated enum variants in `ConfigurationTarget` (e.g., `WorkSpace` -> `Workspace`) and `ProviderType` (e.g., `WorkSpaceSymbol` -> `WorkspaceSymbol`).\n- Refactored all associated `ActionEffect` constructors to match the new naming (e.g., `FindFilesInWorkspace`).\n- Updated struct fields in `ConfigurationInitializationDTO` and `InspectResultDataDTO`.\n\n**New Error Variants:**\n- Added `FeatureNotAvailable`, `TestControllerNotFound`, and `WebViewNotFound` to `CommonError` to provide granular feedback for missing capabilities and resources.\n\n**Maintenance:**\n- Corrected file permissions for Rust source files, removing executable bits (`100755` -> `100644`).\n\n**Impact:** This is a breaking change to the public API of the `Common` crate. Downstream crates (`Mountain`, `Cocoon`, `Wind`) must update their imports and trait implementations to reflect the `Workspace` casing.",
			"SHA": "e622cd0cc20cfb59f863907ede1b4d94ac3c64da"
